    {
      "id": 229055,
      "name": "Sea-Envy",
      "username": "Sea-Envy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/sea-envy/{size}/1849_2.png",
      "created_at": "2019-10-30T13:11:45.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>for completness Nature Guy might also want&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Power - materials - plant</p>\n<p>Principal - principal of flora</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Even if you don't have Minion Maker Archtype you can still get lots of use out of animal control. Natatively you have a pack of wolves as an escort but you have to act on your turn with nature control to have them attack/defend/boost/hinder/overcome for you. They would not be active targets on the feild but a clever enemy could roll to create a \"scattered pack\" persistant hinder on you to lower your rolls when using your beasts</p>\n<p>Duplication Self control power can also be used with out minion maker in this way. Multi Man from Hana Barbera's Imposibles/Super Globtroters was like this- he created copys of himself in collums and rows but they were not independant targets it was almost more like stretching or momentum powers sometimes&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:03:41.776Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
